{
  "metadata": {
    "version": "1.1.0",
    "source": "Health-Assistant Standard Ontology",
    "last_updated": "2026-08-05",
    "description": "Controlled vocabulary of categorical biomarker values (states). Codes are drawn from standard code systems so FHIR interop is immediate: HL7 v3-ObservationInterpretation (POS/NEG/IND/S/R/...), SNOMED CT (Detected/Not detected/Present/Absent), FHIR DataAbsentReason (unknown/not-performed/inconclusive/not-applicable), and a custom URN for proprietary codes (WITHIN_LIMITS / TRACE / STRONGLY_REACTIVE) paralleling CodingSystem.CUSTOM. The catalog is universal (no tenant_id). A BiomarkerDefinition with value_type=state declares its accepted subset via the biomarker_allowed_states join table. States are grouped by category for UI navigation."
  },
